  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/sinumerik.cps`: G83 writes the bottom dwell as `P<ms>`, as on main. The first version of this PR refused the dwell. The maintainer verified the word on a control, so this version removes the refusal. The post output is the same as on main; only the source comment changes.\n- G73, G84 and the G86 dwell refusal do not change. The post writes no G291. It assumes that the control runs in ISO dialect mode.\n- `docs/decisions/2349-sinumerik-g83-dwell.md`: the decision, the sources and the dropped options.\n\n## Readings\n\n- The maintainer, 2026-11-17: \"Can verify the G83 P dwell word works if you run (840D i iso mode (G291))\". Dialog choices: G83 \"Keep P, no refusal\"; P unit \"Yes, milliseconds\"; G73 dwell (#2354) \"Post P as on G83\".\n- Siemens, *SINUMERIK ONE / 840D sl / 828D ISO dialects*, Function Manual, 07/2021. Read: section 6.3 (table 6-2, CYCLE381M, CYCLE383M, CYCLE384M), the shell-cycle GUD list, section 4.2.10 (G04) and SD 55810.\n  - Table 6-2 lists P on G82, G84 and G89. It lists no P on G73, G83, G85 and G86.\n  - The GUD dwell at final depth is for G82, G89, G76 and G87 only.\n  - SD 55810 (dwell in seconds or revolutions for G83/G87) applies to ISO dialect T only.\n- Disagreement: the manual lists no P on G83, but the maintainer saw P work on the control. G83 stays as on main (P in ms).\n- Disagreement: the maintainer chose P on G73, but the manual lists no P on G73, and the control check was for G83 only. G73 stays as on main. #2354 stays open and blocked for the maintainer.\n- Siemens document 109783242: named by the maintainer, not read. The page needs JavaScript and gave no text.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/post/tests/sinumerik_g83_dwell.rs`:\n- `sinumerik_g83_dwell_posts_p_in_ms`\n- `sinumerik_g83_without_dwell_is_unchanged`\n- `sinumerik_g82_dwell_still_posts`\n\nAll `camcraft-post` tests: 74 binaries, 651 passed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -D warnings`: clean. No golden changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run on a real control. The G83 P word rests on the maintainer's check.\n- The `camcraft-app` conformance goldens were not run again. The post output is the same as on main.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2349\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Clarified Sinumerik drilling-cycle dwell behavior: G83 and G82 support dwell values under the documented ISO-dialect assumption, while G73 and G84 remain unchanged.\n  * Added guidance on how G83 dwell values are represented in output and notes on verification for the 840D.\n* **Tests**\n  * Added checks for G83 output with and without dwell, and G82 output with dwell.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
